Collapsible white space takes no layout space where CSS removes it. Collapsible spaces ending a line are removed
from its text, so the line, its shrink-to-fit width, its closed inline boxes, underline and text-overflow end before
them; preserved spaces ending a pre-wrap line hang. Neither makes a word overflow the line, and their width is
measured only for a line end or an overflowing token. White space between inline boxes collapses to one space, and
into a preceding one. An inline container whose lines all collapsed away (white space between block boxes) does not
exist for margin collapsing.
CSS Text 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-text-3/#white-space-phase-1
CSS Text 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-text-3/#white-space-phase-2
CSS 2.2: https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS22/visuren.html#inline-formatting

